643
00:40:37.677 --> 00:40:38.317
1.

644
00:40:38.597 --> 00:40:40.005
Context and Problem.

645
00:40:40.285 --> 00:40:45.107
A Redis-lock leader paused past its TTL and overwrote its successor's settlement:

646
00:40:45.387 --> 00:40:49.291
214 stores were paid twice (§1.1).

647
00:40:49.571 --> 00:40:55.373
Order timelines sorted by wall-clock timestamps from different hosts showed effects before causes.

648
00:40:55.653 --> 00:41:02.501
Several jobs (settlement, reconciliation, bucket mover, report exporters) each had their own ad-hoc locking.

649
00:41:02.781 --> 00:41:03.485
2.

650
00:41:03.765 --> 00:41:05.109
Goals or Non-Goals.

651
00:41:06.459 --> 00:41:21.862
Goals: one standard for exactly one active runner; no write from a deposed leader can take effect; a linearizable store for shard maps and critical config; causal ordering of events across services; clock offsets measured and alerted.

652
00:41:22.142 --> 00:41:31.593
Non-goals: strict serializability across order shards (Ch 13 covers sagas); multi-region consensus (Ch 27).

653
00:41:31.873 --> 00:41:32.619
3.

654
00:41:32.899 --> 00:41:33.859
Requirements.

655
00:41:35.209 --> 00:41:36.575
Here is a quick table:

656
00:41:36.855 --> 00:41:38.327
ID, and Requirement.

657
00:41:38.607 --> 00:41:39.652
NFR-1:

658
00:41:39.932 --> 00:41:47.057
