669
00:42:23.442 --> 00:42:24.146
4.

670
00:42:24.426 --> 00:42:26.538
Capacity and latency estimates.

671
00:42:27.888 --> 00:42:29.253
Here is a quick table:

672
00:42:29.533 --> 00:42:32.669
Item, and Calculation, and Result. etcd data.

673
00:42:32.949 --> 00:42:34.016
Calculation:

674
00:42:34.296 --> 00:42:41.955
Shard map (1,024 keys) + ~200 flags + ~20 election keys + Patroni.

675
00:42:42.235 --> 00:42:43.045
Result:

676
00:42:43.325 --> 00:42:46.141
10 MB (quota 2 GB). etcd writes.

677
00:42:46.421 --> 00:42:47.488
Calculation:

678
00:42:47.768 --> 00:42:48.771
Keep-alives:

679
00:42:49.051 --> 00:42:52.891
30 candidates or 3 s + Patroni + map changes.

680
00:42:53.171 --> 00:42:57.288
Result: ~20 writes per second (trivial). etcd write latency.

681
00:42:57.568 --> 00:42:58.635
Calculation:

682
00:42:58.915 --> 00:43:04.909
Majority round trip cross-AZ ~1 to 2 ms + fsync ~1 to 5 ms.

683
00:43:05.189 --> 00:43:07.621
Result: p99 ~10 ms.

684
00:43:07.901 --> 00:43:08.797
Watches.

685
00:43:09.077 --> 00:43:12.704
Calculation: ~600 pods times 2 watches.

686
00:43:12.984 --> 00:43:16.888
Result: ~1.2 K watches (fine for 3 nodes).

687
00:43:17.168 --> 00:43:18.299
Failover time.

688
00:43:18.579 --> 00:43:19.645
Calculation:

689
00:43:19.925 --> 00:43:24.960
TTL 10 s, keep-alive every 3 s, campaign ~50 ms.

690
00:43:25.240 --> 00:43:27.309
Result: at most ~11 s.

691
00:43:27.589 --> 00:43:28.848
HLC size.

692
00:43:29.128 --> 00:43:30.195
Calculation:

693
00:43:30.475 --> 00:43:33.461
48-bit ms + 16-bit logical.

694
00:43:33.741 --> 00:43:34.552
Result:

695
00:43:34.832 --> 00:43:36.133
8 bytes per event.

696
00:43:37.483 --> 00:43:38.251
5.

697
00:43:38.531 --> 00:43:55.833
Proposed design. etcd, 3 members in 3 AZs (5 in a later phase if maintenance windows show a need), on dedicated SSD-backed VMs, TLS + client certificates, per-job RBAC prefixes, defragmented and snapshotted on a schedule.

698
00:43:56.113 --> 00:43:59.953
Shared with Patroni (separate prefix), monitored as tier-0.

699
00:44:00.233 --> 00:44:09.043
Leader election library (FencedLeadership): lease TTL 10 s, keep-alive 3 s, campaign on a job-specific election name.

700
00:44:09.323 --> 00:44:14.657
Fencing token = the leader key's create revision, which is cluster-wide monotonic.

701
00:44:14.937 --> 00:44:19.715
The leader loop checks leadership before each batch and passes the token into every write.

702
00:44:21.065 --> 00:44:30.281
Resources enforce the fence: tables written by leader-only jobs have a fence bigint column, and every write is... where fence =:token.

703
00:44:30.561 --> 00:44:34.636
A zero-row result means lost leadership: abort and re-campaign.

704
00:44:34.916 --> 00:44:39.780
External side effects go through an idempotent outbox, never straight from the leader.

705
00:44:40.060 --> 00:44:51.196
Shard map and flags in etcd, updated only with transactions (If(modRevision == expected)), and read through watches starting at the revision last seen.

706
00:44:52.546 --> 00:45:00.887
HLC in the event envelope (hlc: ms.logical), sent on every outgoing call and message, merged on receipt.

707
00:45:01.167 --> 00:45:04.133
Timelines sort by HLC, then event id.

708
00:45:04.413 --> 00:45:18.599
Clock policy: chrony against the cloud time service, makestep only at boot, offset exported as a metric, and every timeout and duration uses System.nanoTime (a lint rule bans currentTimeMillis differences).

709
00:45:18.879 --> 00:45:19.626
7.

710
00:45:19.906 --> 00:45:21.421
