On screen: == 1. cluster status. e1: raft term 2, LEADER. e2: raft term 2, follower. e3: raft term 2, follower. == 2. leader election with a lease; the leader key's createrevision is the fencing. token. pod-A campaigns (lease TTL 3 s, keep-alive running), then token 2. pod-B campaigns,

960
01:07:24.046 --> 01:07:49.262
then lost (and keeps its own lease alive, retrying). pod-A freezes (SIGSTOP on its keep-alive process). leader key gone after 3233 ms (lease expired on the etcd leader's clock). pod-B campaigns again, then token 4. pod-A wakes; its keep-alive now reports: lease 6ca3a0d869c49308 already expired.

961
01:07:49.542 --> 01:07:56.582
PostgreSQL: pod-B writes with token 4, then 1 row; pod-A writes with token 2, then 0 rows.

962
01:07:56.862 --> 01:07:58.377
The rest is in the chapter.

963
01:08:01.227 --> 01:08:07.008
Election and fencing, end to end: pod B's campaign fails while pod A's lease is alive.

964
01:08:07.288 --> 01:08:15.928
Pod A's keep-alive is frozen, and the etcd leader's clock expires the lease about 3.2 s later (the TTL is 3 s).

965
01:08:16.208 --> 01:08:19.344
Pod B wins with token 4 against A's token 2.

966
01:08:19.624 --> 01:08:27.944
When A wakes, etcd tells it the lease is gone, but A's stale write had already been sent and was rejected by PostgreSQL (0 rows).

967
01:08:28.224 --> 01:08:31.275
The fence is what protected the data, not A noticing.

968
01:08:31.555 --> 01:08:42.435
Failover: killing the Raft leader (SIGKILL, a crash) produced a new leader in ~2.4 s: the randomized 1 to 2 s election timeout plus detection.

969
01:08:42.715 --> 01:08:45.424
The term went from 2 to 3, and writes resumed.

970
01:08:46.774 --> 01:08:52.129
Quorum loss is CP: alone, a member refuses writes and linearizable reads.

971
01:08:52.409 --> 01:08:59.918
It will answer a serializable read, and here it returned after-failover although v2 had been acknowledged to a client earlier.

972
01:09:00.198 --> 01:09:05.510
That's a real stale read, the etcd version of leader answers from local state in L3.

973
01:09:05.790 --> 01:09:08.521
After healing, the same member returns v2.

974
01:09:08.801 --> 01:09:11.254
CAS: two movers read modrevision 9.

975
01:09:11.534 --> 01:09:16.142
The first transaction succeeds, and the second fails because the revision changed.

976
01:09:16.422 --> 01:09:19.281
Exactly one flip wins, with no lock needed.

977
01:09:20.631 --> 01:09:28.417
Watches: a watch from revision + 1 replays every change since the snapshot, so nothing falls between load and watch.

978
01:09:28.697 --> 01:09:33.561
After compaction, the watch is cancelled with required revision has been compacted.

979
01:09:33.841 --> 01:09:36.721
That's why L4's loadAndWatch has a resync path.

