1146
01:18:27.341 --> 01:18:32.909
Security. etcd holds the keys to the kingdom (shard maps, leader keys, Patroni state).

1147
01:18:33.189 --> 01:18:38.991
Use mutual TLS, per-client certificates, RBAC per key prefix, and network isolation.

1148
01:18:39.271 --> 01:18:43.858
Encrypt snapshots, and never expose the client port outside the cluster network.

1149
01:18:44.138 --> 01:18:48.298
A client that can write or elections or settlement can make itself leader.

1150
01:18:48.578 --> 01:18:52.567
RBAC must restrict election prefixes to the job's identity.

1151
01:18:52.847 --> 01:19:01.957
Fencing tokens aren't secrets, but the fence column must only be writable through the fenced path (no ad-hoc scripts that reset fence = 0).

1152
01:19:03.307 --> 01:19:04.864
